/**
\page tiffdump_lane iccTiffDump: TIFF metadata and ICC inspection lane

\tableofcontents

\section tiffdump_cli Options and positional arguments

`iccTiffDump` parses `--evidence-json`, `--ifd N`, `--list-directories`, and
telemetry options before rebuilding `argv` from the remaining positional
tokens. Options may appear before or after the TIFF path. The reduced `argc`
is 2 for inspection or listing, or 3 when a single-directory ICC extraction
destination is supplied:

| Reduced token | Name | Contract |
|---|---|---|
| `argv[0]` | program | Invocation name |
| `argv[1]` | tiff_file | Source classic TIFF or BigTIFF |
| `argv[2]` | exported_icc_file | Optional extraction destination, single-IFD mode only |

`--ifd N` accepts a zero-based main-chain index from 0 through 4095 and
defaults to 0. `--list-directories` inventories up to 4096 main-chain IFDs;
it cannot be combined with `--ifd` or extraction. Listing includes SubIFD
offsets without following them. Single-directory inspection does not
inventory or validate the rest of the main chain.

\dotfile tiffdump-lane.dot "iccTiffDump option parsing and inspection modes"

\section tiffdump_help Reporting and output

A bare invocation or `--help` prints usage and exits 0; `--help` is recognized
at any argument position and short-circuits further parsing. `--version` must
be used alone. Other malformed invocations return status 1 and print usage on
stderr when the positional count is wrong. Inspection reads metadata
only: codec availability, directory fields, and ICC tags are reported through
libtiff, but pixels are not decoded or validated. `--evidence-json` changes
the report format without changing the inspection scope.

An extraction destination is written through a sibling temporary file and
atomically renamed after the complete byte copy. The raw ICC bytes are kept
for forensics even if a later IccProfLib parse fails; that later failure still
returns nonzero. Telemetry-enabled builds record one selected directory in
inspection mode or visited directory counts in listing mode. Every help and
version banner includes the linked libtiff runtime version.

See \ref tiff_processing_pipeline "TIFF image processing pipeline" for the
cross-tool view and `Tools/CmdLine/IccTiffDump/Readme.md` for report fields
and diagnostic interpretation.
*/
